<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bardo National Museum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bardo National Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, opened in 1888 in a former palace of the Husainid beys, is the national archaeological museum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. It holds one of the world's largest collections of Roman mosaics, gathered from sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dougga">Dougga</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-djem">El Djem</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sousse">Sousse</a>, including the famous portrait of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a>. In March 2015 an attack by gunmen there killed more than twenty people.</p></div>
